    "q-65311": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65311",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ \n\nI. The range of the function is $[-1,1]$\n\nII. The function is increasing on the interval $(0,\\pi ).$\n\nIII. The function doesn't have a maximum value.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264709/assets/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is decreasing on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and increasing on the interval $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ).$ Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statement III is true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
